{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeshDyXoWf5AUJMCATdxK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I now have a complete understanding of the repository structure and conventions. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add a `status` field to the Order data class with type `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED). New orders are ACTIVE by default.\n\n2. **OrderStatus.kt** (new enum file) - Define the OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add a method `findByOrderIdIn(orderIds: List<String>): List<Order>` (for consistency, though not strictly needed yet). Actually, we need a method to find all shipments by orderId, but that belongs in ShipmentRepository.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add method `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** - Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist (using ResourceNotFoundException)\n   - Returns 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (using ConflictException with new error code ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED)\n   - Sets order status to CANCELLED and cancels all CREATED shipments if order is ACTIVE\n   - Returns the updated order with 200 status\n   - Returns the order unchanged if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** - Modify the create endpoint to check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If cancelled, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED error code.\n\n7. **ApiError.kt** - Add error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for creating shipment on cancelled order), `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` (for cancel blocked by confirmed shipment).\n\n8. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Cancel an active order with created shipments\n   - Cancel already cancelled order (idempotent)\n   - Cancel blocked by confirmed shipment\n   - Cancel non-existent order\n   - Verify GET returns cancelled status\n   - Verify shipment creation on cancelled order fails\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using a service layer for business logic: Rejected because the existing codebase has all logic in the controller layer, and maintaining consistency is more important than adding abstraction.\n- Adding an error code for \"order not found during cancel\": Not needed, ResourceNotFoundException is already defined and consistent.\n- Creating a separate OrderService class: Rejected to maintain architectural consistency with the existing pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Successful cancel of ACTIVE order:*\n1. Client calls POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. OrderController receives request\n3. Check if order exists (throw 404 if not)\n4. Check if any shipment has CONFIRMED status (throw 409 with ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED if true)\n5. Set order.status = CANCELLED\n6. Find all shipments with status CREATED for this order\n7. Set each CREATED shipment.status = CANCELLED\n8. Save updated order to repository\n9. Save all updated shipments to repository\n10. Return order with status code 200\n\n*Idempotent cancel of already CANCELLED order:*\n1. Client calls POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Order exists with status CANCELLED\n3. No validation errors\n4. Return order as-is with status code 200\n\n*Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment:*\n1. Client calls POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Order exists with status ACTIVE\n3. Check shipments: find CONFIRMED status\n4. Throw ConflictException (409) with ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED\n5. Nothing changes in database\n\n*Creating shipment for CANCELLED order:*\n1. Client calls POST /shipments with orderId of cancelled order\n2. OrderRepository.findById returns the order\n3. Check if order.status == CANCELLED\n4. Throw ConflictException (409) with ORDER_CANCELLED\n5. Nothing saved\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **test_cancel_active_order_cancels_created_shipments** - Create order and multiple shipments (CREATED status), cancel order, verify order is CANCELLED and shipments are CANCELLED\n2. **test_cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds** - Cancel an order twice, second cancel should succeed and return same order\n3. **test_cancel_fails_with_confirmed_shipment** - Create order with CONFIRMED shipment, attempt cancel, verify 409 and order/shipment unchanged\n4. **test_cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404** - Cancel non-existent order, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n5. **test_get_order_includes_status** - Create order, verify GET returns status field\n6. **test_cannot_create_shipment_for_cancelled_order** - Create and cancel order, attempt to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":827,"cache_read_input_tokens":19378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":827},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f4c6aaf-eb2d-4a93-92e9-c5e336f39618","uuid":"ca695253-a145-4faa-b710-802e835708e6","timestamp":"2026-09-09T10:18:26.462Z","request_id":"req_011CeshDxqPD4xxE74umn6f7"}
