s` field and OrderStatus enum to track order lifecycle\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with full business logic\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by order\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added order cancellation check when creating shipments\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 8 comprehensive tests covering cancel behavior, status field, and error cases\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 2 tests for shipment creation on cancelled/active orders\n\nTests:\n- test_cancel_active_order_returns_200_and_changes_status_to_CANCELLED: Verifies cancel returns 200 and updates status\n- test_cancel_persists_the_order_as_CANCELLED: Verifies persisted state survives GET retrieval\n- test_cancel_cancels_all_CREATED_shipments: Verifies all CREATED shipments transition to CANCELLED\n- test_cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotently: Verifies retry succeeds without error\n- test_cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404_with_ORDER_NOT_FOUND: Verifies 404 with proper error code\n- test_cancel_fails_with_409_if_any_shipment_is_CONFIRMED: Verifies 409 when CONFIRMED shipment exists\n- test_cancel_does_not_cancel_CONFIRMED_shipments: Verifies all-or-nothing behavior - nothing changes on rejection\n- test_creates_an_order_with_ACTIVE_status: Verifies new orders default to ACTIVE\n- test_get_returns_order_with_status: Verifies GET response includes status field\n- test_rejects_creating_shipment_for_cancelled_order_with_409_ORDER_CANCELLED: Verifies 409 when creating shipment on cancelled order\n- test_allows_creating_shipment_for_active_order: Verifies shipment creation still works for active orders\n\nVerification: `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ completed successfully with all 24 tests passing (13 order tests, 7 shipment tests, 3 customer tests, 1 application test)\n\nNot done: Nothing - all ticket requirements implemented, tested, and